<span class="tag">Legal</span>
<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
<p>We do not ask you to sign up for anything, and we do not sell your data. Here is exactly what happens to your information when you read this site.</p>
</div></section>

<section class="section"><div class="wrap">
<div class="prose">

<p><strong>Last updated: August 30, 2026</strong></p>

<h2>The short version</h2>
<ul>
<li>We do not ask you to create an account to read anything on this site.</li>
<li>We do not ask for your name, email address, or payment details.</li>
<li>We do not sell your personal information.</li>
<li>The only third party that may set advertising cookies here is Google, which serves the ads.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Who we are</h2>
<p>CopyTools is an independent review site for AI copywriting tools. We test each tool ourselves on real writing work, then publish what happened. This policy explains what information is handled when you visit.</p>
<p>If anything here is unclear, <a href="mailto:{{MAIL_OBF}}">{{MAIL_OBF}}</a> and ask. We answer.</p>

<h2>Information we collect</h2>

<h3>Information you give us</h3>
<p>Only one way exists: you email us. If you do, we have your email address and whatever you wrote. We use it to reply to you and for nothing else. We do not add you to a mailing list, because we do not run one.</p>

<h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
<p>Like nearly every website, our hosting provider records basic request data when your browser loads a page. That can include your IP address, browser and device type, the page you asked for, the page that sent you here, and the time of the request.</p>
<p>This is used to keep the site running and to see which reviews people actually read. It is not used to identify you personally, and we do not combine it with anything you email us.</p>

<h2>Cookies and advertising</h2>
<p>We fund this site with advertising served by Google AdSense.</p>
<p>Google, and the vendors it works with, use cookies to serve ads based on your past visits to this website or other websites. Google's advertising cookies let it and its partners build a picture of your interests and show you ads accordingly.</p>
<p><strong>You can turn this off.</strong> Visit <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow">Google Ads Settings</a> to opt out of personalised advertising, or <a href="https://optout.aboutads.info/" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow">aboutads.info</a> to opt out of third-party advertising cookies more broadly.</p>
<p>If you are in the EU, UK, or another region that requires consent, a consent notice is shown before non-essential cookies are set. Blocking cookies in your browser will not stop you from reading any part of this site; the reviews are never behind a cookie wall.</p>

<h2>Analytics</h2>
<p>We count page views so we know which reviews are worth expanding. We do not use analytics to build profiles of individual readers, and we do not track you across other websites.</p>

<h2>Outbound links and affiliate disclosure</h2>
<p>Our reviews link out to the tools we test. Those are third-party websites with their own privacy policies, and we are not responsible for what they do once you leave this site. Read their policies before you sign up for anything.</p>
<p>Where a link to a tool earns us a commission, we say so on that page. A commission never changes the verdict: if a tool fails our test, it fails in print.</p>

<h2>How we use information</h2>
<ul>
<li>To serve pages and keep the site online.</li>
<li>To reply when you contact us.</li>
<li>To see which reviews get read, so we know what to write next.</li>
<li>To serve and measure advertising.</li>
</ul>
<p>We do not use it to profile you, and we do not hand it to anyone for money.</p>

<h2>How long we keep things</h2>
<p>Server request logs are kept by our hosting provider for a limited period and then discarded. Emails you send us are kept as long as the conversation is useful, and you can ask us to delete them at any time.</p>

<h2>Children's privacy</h2>
<p>This site is written for working adults and is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect information from children. If you believe a child has sent us personal information, <a href="mailto:{{MAIL_OBF}}">{{MAIL_OBF}}</a> and we will delete it.</p>

<h2>Your rights</h2>
<p>Depending on where you live, you may have the right to ask what we hold about you, to have it corrected, to have it deleted, or to tell us to stop using it. To make any of those requests, <a href="mailto:{{MAIL_OBF}}">{{MAIL_OBF}}</a>. We will action it.</p>
<p>If you are a California resident: we do not sell personal information as that term is defined under the CCPA.</p>

<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
<p>If we change how we handle information, we update this page and move the date at the top. Changes take effect the moment they are posted here.</p>

<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>Questions about any of the above: <a href="mailto:{{MAIL_OBF}}">{{MAIL_OBF}}</a>.</p>

</div></div></section>

